      "content": "<p>I made a public notebook where I try to just predict test.csv: <a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/antonkratz/notebookdf0d07f28b\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kaggle.com/code/antonkratz/notebookdf0d07f28b</a></p>\n<p>I reach about 79 tokens/second. I believe that a GTX Blackwell 6000 should reach almost 2000 tokens/second.</p>\n<p>How can I use vllm with the official Kaggle infrastructure? I tried many different ways and workarounds, it seems not possible to install it. How can we best make use of the GTX Blackwell 6000 at full speed? I am orders of magnitude off in the current setup. I believe that I am not the only one facing this.</p>",
